{"name":"Sweet Romance","hex":"#ffc4dd","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sweet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Tasting of sugars.","Retaining a portion of sugar."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used as a positive response to good news or information."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sweet"},{"term":"romance","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An intimate relationship between two people; a love affair.","A strong obsession or attachment for something or someone."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To woo; to court.","To write or tell romantic stories, poetry, letters, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/romance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Romance","blocks":[{"text":"Romance and romantic love encompass a number of ideas about love, which are interrelated for historical and cultural reasons:"},{"items":["passionate feelings of attraction—a mental state of \"being in love\", with focused attention (salience) towards a specific individual for courtship or pair bonding;","the cultural practice or idealization of initiating intimate relationships for feelings like these, over more practical or ordinary concerns;","a relationship or love affair initiated or maintained this way, which may be premarital or absent a commitment; and","a love story involving these elements."]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Frank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg/330px-Frank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Romance","wikidata":"Q1189047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Frank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg/500px-Frank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Frank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg/500px-Frank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Romeo and Juliet, by Frank Dicksee, considered to be the archetypal romantic couple, depicting the play's iconic balcony scene","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFrank_Bernard_Dicksee_-_Romeo_and_Juliet%2C_1884.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png/500px-Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png/500px-Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dopamine is produced in the ventral tegmental area (VTA) of the brain, and projected to the nucleus accumbens (NAc). Dopamine activity in the NAc is key to the attribution of salience.[84]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg/500px-Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg/1280px-Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg/500px-Colour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AColour_Wheel_of_Love.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Crystaled_salt_on_the_stick.jpg/500px-Crystaled_salt_on_the_stick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai